  "slug": "juneteenth-red-punch-strawberry-lemonade-recipe-11738621",
  "name": "Juneteenth 'Red Punch' Strawberry Lemonade",
  "recipe_type": "drink",
  "brief_description": "This Juneteenth \"Red Punch\" strawberry lemonade recipe is easy to make and offers a new, puckering and pleasing twist to the traditional red soda water that has been made in Texas since 1937.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Gather all ingredients."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Add strawberries, sugar, lemonade concentrate, and water to a blender in that order. Pulse the mixture a few times. Then blend at low speed for 2 minutes. Gradually turn the speed up to medium. Blend until smooth."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Pour strawberry lemonade into a large pitcher or punch bowl. Serve over ice. Recipe courtesy of Angela Shelf Medearis, author of The New African-American Kitchen , The Kitchen Diva Cooks! , and The Kitchen Diva\u2019s Diabetic Cookbook . Taken from Opal Lee and What it Means to Be Free, written by Alice Faye Duncan and illustrated by Keturah A. Bobo. Text Copyright \u00a9 2022 by Alice Faye Duncan. Art Copyright \u00a9 2022 by Keturah A. Bobo. Used by permission of HarperCollins Christian Publishing ."
    }
  ],
